1
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:13,910
♪ Led through the mist ♪

2
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:17,070
♪ by the milk light of moon ♪

3
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:23,040
♪ all that was lost is revealed ♪

4
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,290
♪ our long-bygone burdens ♪

5
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:29,880
♪ mere echoes of the spring ♪

6
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:33,260
♪ but where have we come ♪

7
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:36,760
♪ and where shall we end? ♪

8
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,890
♪ if dreams can't come true ♪

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:46,430
♪ then why not pretend? ♪

10
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:50,080
♪ how the gentle wind ♪

11
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:53,380
♪ beckons through the leaves ♪

12
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:59,910
♪ as autumn colors fall ♪

13
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,660
Somewhere lost in the clouded annals of history

14
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:07,820
lies a place that few have seen...

15
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:11,970
a mysterious place called th{ Unknown,

16
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:15,470
where long-forgotten stories are revealed to those

17
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:18,680
who travel through the wood.

18
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:19,930
...Antelope, Guggenheim,

19
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:24,000
Albert, Salami, Giggly, Jumpy, Tom, Thomas, Tambourine,

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,110
Leg face McCullen, Artichoke, Penguin, Pete, Steve,

21
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:32,370
but I think the very worst name for this frog is...

22
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:35,530
Wait. Wait a second. Uh, Greg...

23
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:43,370
...where are we?

24
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:44,370
In the woods.

25
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:45,370
I mean

26
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:47,290
what are we doing out here?

27
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:48,420
We're walking home.

28
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:50,040
Greg, I think we're lost.

29
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,750
We sh... we should have left a trail or something.

30
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:54,340
I can leave a trail of candy from my pants.

31
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,220
No.

32
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:59,920
Though I am lost, my wounded heart resides back home,

33
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,590
in pieces, strewn about the graveyard of my lost love,

34
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,960
for only...

35
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:06,640
Huh! Do you hear that?

36
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:07,640
Yeah.

37
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,360
Do you think it's some kind of deranged lunatic with an ax

38
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,650
waiting out there in the darkness for innocent victims?

39
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:14,230
Greg. Greg!

40
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,450
Greg, you're gonna get us into trouble again.

41
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:26,820
We should ask him for help.

42
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,220
No, we should not ask him for help.

43
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:28,960
- But...
- Shh!

44
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:29,530
You shush.

45
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,960
- You shush.
- Shh.

46
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,060
Shoot.

47
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,920
You think we should have asked him for help?

48
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,300
Maybe I can help you?

49
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,470
I mean, you guys are lost, right?

50
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,180
What in the world is going on?

51
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:46,830
Well, you're slapping yourself

52
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:48,790
and I'm answering your question and...

53
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:52,610
No, Greg. A bird's brain isn't big enough for cognizant speech.

54
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:53,610
Hey, what was that?

55
00:02:53,610 --> 00:02:55,970
I mean, I'm just saying you're... you're weird...

56
00:02:55,970 --> 00:02:57,570
like, not normal. I-I mean..

57
00:02:57,570 --> 00:02:59,200
Oh, my gosh. Stop talking to it, Wirt.

58
00:02:59,200 --> 00:02:59,740
"It"?

59
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:00,310
Uh... uh...

60
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,700
What are you doing here?!

61
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:03,030
Explain yourselves!

62
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,480
And I'll see you guys later. Bye.

63
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:06,200
Calm... calm down, mister.

64
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,920
Wh-Whatever you do here is your business.

65
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,210
We just want to get home

66
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:10,710
with all of our legs and arms attached.

67
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:13,210
These woods are no place for children.

68
00:03:13,210 --> 00:03:15,630
Don't you know the beast is afoot here?

69
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,460
The beast?

70
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,080
W-W-W-We don't know anything about that.

71
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,760
W-We're just two lost kids trying to get home.

72
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,260
Well, welcome to the Unknown, boys.

73
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:24,390
You're more lost than you realize.

74
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,690
I found this homestead abandoned

75
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:35,230
and re-purposed its mill for my needs.

76
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:40,530
You and your brother should be safe here, while I work.

77
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:43,870
Candy trail, candy trail, candy trail.

78
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:46,580
What... what is your work, exactly?

79
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:50,250
Everyone has a torch to burn,

80
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:51,910
and this here's mine.

81
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:55,410
I grind the horrid edelwood trees

82
00:03:55,410 --> 00:03:58,170
into oil to keep this lantern lit.

83
00:03:58,170 --> 00:04:00,670
This is my lot in life.

84
00:04:00,670 --> 00:04:02,470
This is my burden.

85
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:03,760
This guy sounds loony.

86
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,100
Maybe we should make a break for it, if we can.

87
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:07,430
But he must know the woods really well

88
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:08,930
so we may need to knock him out first

89
00:04:08,930 --> 00:04:10,800
Except that may turn out really badly, huh?

90
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,020
Yeah, bad... bad plan.

91
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,850
- Forget it. Bad plan.
- Okay.

92
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,690
What are you boys whispering about?

93
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,690
We're talking about running away out of here.

94
00:04:17,690 --> 00:04:18,690
Shh! Shh!

95
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:20,000
- Shh!
- Shh!

96
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:23,650
Leave if you wish. But remember...

97
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:26,620
the beast haunts these woods,

98
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:30,870
ever singing his mournful melody

99
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:33,540
in search of lost souls such as yourselves!

100
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,540
- To help us?
- No, not to help you.

101
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:37,840
I have work to do in the mill.

102
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:40,840
When I am finished, I will do what I can to guide you

103
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,840
if you are still here when I return.

104
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,850
Huh, I guess we could just leave.

105
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,520
But I don't know.

106
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,760
Greg!

107
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,880
What?

108
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,190
Do you really think there is a beast out there?

109
00:04:56,190 --> 00:04:58,190
Or is that guy just messing with us?

110
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,610
Uh huh.

111
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:03,250
I mean, he could have done away with us by now if that was his plan

112
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:04,610
and he lit that fire.

113
00:05:04,610 --> 00:05:06,360
- That's pretty nice.
- Yeah!

114
00:05:06,370 --> 00:05:08,210
I guess it's possible there's a beast,

115
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:10,850
since there was a talking bird, but...
- Yeah!

116
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:12,810
I don't know.

117
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,460
Sometimes I feel like I'm just like...

118
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:18,290
a boat upon a winding river,

119
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:21,300
twisting towards an endless black sea...

120
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,380
further and further

121
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,800
drifting away from where I want to be,

122
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,800
who I want to be.

123
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,940
Oh. I didn't know that.

124
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:32,420
Did you know that if you soak a raisin in grape juice, it turns into a grape?

125
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,560
It's a rock fact!

126
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:36,310
You're not helping at all.

127
00:05:36,310 --> 00:05:38,560
Why don't you go play with your frog or something?

128
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,590
Aw, beans!

129
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:41,400
Where is that frog o' mine?

130
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,760
Hold on there, second brother o' mine.

131
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,920
I'll be back soon for your plan.

132
00:05:52,910 --> 00:05:54,660
Kitty? Kitty!

133
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,660
Now, where did that frog named "Kitty" go?

134
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:57,670
Whoop!

135
00:05:57,670 --> 00:06:00,670
I tripped on my own candy trail!

136
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,590
Huh?

137
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,470
graawr

138
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,800
That frog's giving me the runaround.

139
00:06:15,370 --> 00:06:16,390
Kitty!

140
00:06:30,310 --> 00:06:31,250
Gross.

141
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:32,120
graawr

142
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:32,950
Kitty?

143
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,060
Hmm. Is that...

144
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:38,750
Whoop!

145
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,070
Oh, there you are!

146
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,750
graawr

147
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:43,340
Wirt?

148
00:06:46,050 --> 00:06:46,840
Kitty?

149
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,760
You have beautiful eyes.

150
00:06:57,020 --> 00:06:57,680
Greg?

151
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,180
Uh...

152
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:03,610
What's happening?!

153
00:07:03,610 --> 00:07:04,880
Where's your brother?!

154
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,110
Uh-uh-uh.

155
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:09,200
Holy moly. Hot dog.

156
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:13,120
It's the beast!

157
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,030
Stay back, boys!

158
00:07:15,030 --> 00:07:17,010
This creature which is known as...

159
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:17,700
Huh?

160
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,620
Ohhh.

161
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:22,120
Greg, why did you do that?!

162
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,620
That was your plan, remember?

163
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:24,560
Knock him out!

164
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,770
No! Bad plan!

165
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,050
I told you to forget that plan!

166
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:32,030
Spank! Spank! Spank!

167
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:36,140
Run, run, run, run, run, run, run!

168
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:40,020
Candy camouflage!

169
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,560
Run, run, run, run, run, run, run, run.

170
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,070
- Greg!
- This is amazing, huh?!

171
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,460
Am I supposed to throw something?

172
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,660
Oof.

173
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,870
Oh, yeah!

174
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:03,370
Ha ha!

175
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:05,910
He's eating your candy.

176
00:08:05,910 --> 00:08:09,420
I wonder if he ate my whole candy trail that led to this mill.

177
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,670
Ugh! Greg

178
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:13,590
you led the beast right to us with your candy!

179
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:23,270
Hey, give me the ax.

180
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:24,770
You're too little to have it anyway. I-

181
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:27,690
Ahhh, w-we got to get out of here!

182
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:39,490
Ah! Uh, Greg, give him the rest of your candy!

183
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:45,830
Oops.

184
00:08:58,930 --> 00:09:00,140
Hey, Wirt, look!

185
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:00,620
Greg?

186
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:04,000
Wirt, he spit up that turtle, and now he's my new best friend!

187
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:05,780
Ohh! Ohh.

188
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,310
Hey, where are you going?

189
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,650
Ain't that just the way...

190
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:13,860
The mill is destroyed. The oil...

191
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,320
all gone!

192
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:18,950
But... but... but look. We got the beast problem solved.

193
00:09:20,450 --> 00:09:23,620
The dog?! That is not the beast!

194
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:27,960
The beast cannot be mollified like some farmer's pet!

195
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:31,050
He stalks like the night.

196
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:33,050
He sings like the four winds.

197
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:35,630
He is the death of hope.

198
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:37,260
He steals their children,

199
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:41,510
and he'll... ruin...

200
00:09:41,510 --> 00:09:43,520
You're always messing up, Greg.

201
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,350
Boy!

202
00:09:44,350 --> 00:09:46,350
you have it backwards!

203
00:09:46,350 --> 00:09:48,900
You are the elder child!

204
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:53,480
You are responsible for you and your brother's actions!

205
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:56,870
I'm... I'm... I'm sorry. Maybe I can... fix it?

206
00:09:56,870 --> 00:09:57,990
I-I can't fix it.

207
00:09:58,290 --> 00:09:59,990
You must go.

208
00:09:59,990 --> 00:10:02,700
Take your brother North. Look for a town.

209
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,790
Yeah. Thanks. Come on, Greg.

210
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:06,910
One last thing.

211
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:09,420
beware the Unknown!

212
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:13,340
Fear the beast and leave these woods...

213
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,170
if you can.

214
00:10:15,570 --> 00:10:19,180
It is your burden to bear!

215
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,890
Right. Yeah. Got it.

216
00:10:20,890 --> 00:10:23,890
And, little one, you look after that frog.

217
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:25,890
Give him a proper name.

218
00:10:25,890 --> 00:10:27,230
graawr

219
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:27,980
Okay.

220
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:36,320
Wirt, I think I thought of a new name for our frog.

221
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,320
I'm gonna call him "Wirt."

222
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,910
That's gonna be really confusing.

223
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:42,160
No, I'm gonna call you "Kitty."

224
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:42,820
What?!

225
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,910
Maybe I'll start calling you "candy pants."

226
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:46,400
Whoa! Yeah!

227
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,480
graawr

228
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,750
Good one, Wirt.

229
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,460
Thanks.

230
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,090
I'm not talking to you.

231
00:10:51,090 --> 00:10:52,470
I'm talking to Wirt.
